<title>ESTONIA: TALLINNA PANK TAKES NEW BOARD MEMBER.</title>
<headline>TALLINNA PANK TAKES NEW BOARD MEMBER.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tallinna Pank said on Thursday that it has taken Gunnar Okk as it new development director and board member.</p>
<p>In a statement, the bank said that Okk, 36, will join the bank's board and will be responsible for the group's marketing, public relations and quality.</p>
<p>Okk had previously worked as managing director for Statoil Eesti, the Norwegian state oil company subsidairy in Estonia.</p>
<p>-- Tallinn newsroom +372 630 8400 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
